{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers","id":974509,"title":"How Flexible are kindred powers ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-22T10:33:45-07:00","id":974509,"title":"How Flexible are kindred powers ?","content":"I wanted to know how flexible are kindred powers ?<br /> <br /> When you read them you see each one has a set effect. I wanted to know can you bend some of these effects a bit to do things the original power did not state ?<br /> <br /> Example <br /> <br /> Iron Edict<br /> <br /> Could rather then using it on yourself to make yourself not be scared or even make yourself believe your stronger ?<br /> <br /> like in the anime Rurouni Kenshin where Kenshin was fighting Kurogasa?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:42:16-07:00","id":974518,"title":"","content":"Disciplines are generally not flexible at all.<br /> <br /> If you want them to do something new, that is usually the domain of Devotions.<br /> <br /> Your specific example has been a matter of debate that I'll leave up to other people to comment on.<br /> <br /> Whether you are a valid target for your own Domination powers has come up before. I think the usual consensus is that you can, but I can't speak for certain on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:06:00-07:00","id":974543,"title":"","content":"I'm in the &quot;no, you can't dominate yourself&quot; camp. First of all you need eye contact, though that's possible with a mirror. The bigger concern is that every command or instruction you can deliver with Dominate requires the subject to be under the Mezmerized Condition, and once you're Mezmerized, you're in command-receiving mode, not command-giving mode. I just don't see a Mezmerized character as being in any fit state of mind to use Dominate.<br /> <br /> And yeah. Disciplines are pretty rigid, they just do what they do. If you can think of clever ways to utilize what they do, awesome, but you can't really change their base functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:00:12-07:00","id":974571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers?p=974543#post974543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in the &quot;no, you can't dominate yourself&quot; camp. First of all you need eye contact, though that's possible with a mirror. The bigger concern is that every command or instruction you can deliver with Dominate requires the subject to be under the Mezmerized Condition, and once you're Mezmerized, you're in command-receiving mode, not command-giving mode. I just don't see a Mezmerized character as being in any fit state of mind to use Dominate.<br /> <br /> And yeah. Disciplines are pretty rigid, they just do what they do. If you can think of clever ways to utilize what they do, awesome, but you can't really change their base functions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that disciplines do what they say they do and to make them do additional or stronger things that you need to create a devotion.<br /> <br /> I do not think you can dominate yourself. First. Dominating someone crushes their will to the point where you impose your will upon them. If you crush your own will, how are you strong enough to give commands.... Like Charlaquin said, you are in command-receiving mode, not giving. You cant have your cake and eat it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:09:34-07:00","id":974581,"title":"","content":"Yes and no. Normally deviations from the descriptions are the purview of devotions and usually require multiple disciplines that contribute the desired effect and for the user to possess those disciplines at the respective level beforehand as pre-requisites to learn them. However, there are also single discipline devotions and those allow discipline progression to branch slightly into a different direction and usually have that discipline at the given level as a prerequisite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-23-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:28:41-07:00","id":974593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers?p=974543#post974543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate requires the subject to be under the Mezmerized Condition, and once you're Mezmerized, you're in command-receiving mode, not command-giving mode. I just don't see a Mezmerized character as being in any fit state of mind to use Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question about your interpretation: Would say then it is impossible for a vampire which is Mesmerized and also has Dominate to successfully use Dominate to Mesmerize another third party?<br /> <br /> Vampire A Mesmerizes Vampire B, and thus by your interpretation as I understand it, Vampire B can not be successfully commanded to Mesmerize Vampire C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:31:05-07:00","id":974595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers?p=974593#post974593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about your interpretation: Would say then it is impossible for a vampire which is Mesmerized and also has Dominate to successfully use Dominate to Mesmerize another third party?<br /> <br /> Vampire A Mesmerizes Vampire B, and thus Vampire B can not be successfully commanded to Mesmerize Vampire C.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, except through the Devotion <i>Chain of Command</i>, and even then it's technically Vampire A giving the command, just using Vampire B as a proxy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:50:44-07:00","id":974607,"title":"","content":"Well - you could do that, but it does slightly stifle the rule of cool to limit disciplines by not allowing innovative uses. I would say in general yes, for extremely outlandish uses if you want to use it regularly in a certain way (like the self imposition of a condition) a devotion is the way to go. However, for a sudden flash of genius - like a player trying the above in a moment of desperation, or using celerity to check the pistol in a game of Russian roulette with no-one noticing, or obfuscate to hide the taste of your blood in a rival's wine - I would encourage them to be creative, charging them at most a willpower for the improvisation.<br /> <br /> If you want a regular new power, perhaps a devotion is in order. If you have a cool idea that enhances play directly and doesn't break theme, I try to be a bit more loosey goosey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:00:50-07:00","id":974617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers?p=974607#post974607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well - you could do that, but it does slightly stifle the rule of cool to limit disciplines by not allowing innovative uses.<br /> <br /> I try to be a bit more loosey goosey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you are saying, but another way to look at &quot;innovative uses&quot; is that if they are all Devotions then the innovation effort put in by the vampire that perfects the technique is a type of Capital which then has value due to exclusivity and marketability. Post-Scarcity of Innovation (ie loosey-goosey use of disciplines) spoils the rule of cool for having a high-intrigue investment/reward economy of trade secrets being bartered. People, especially players, like having nifty things no one else have and niche but not overly powerful Devotions make a lot of room for that.<br /> <br /> High functioning, reactive, and complex economies and ecosystems in game enrich the experience and immersion. Not to say you are wrong with the bounty you freely give away, just showing the other side of the coin where scarcity of innovation also has value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-22-2016, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:04:15-07:00","id":974621,"title":"","content":"I don't disagree at all; a different style of play.<br /> <br /> More power to the pair of us!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:16:46-07:00","id":974632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers?p=974607#post974607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well - you could do that, but it does slightly stifle the rule of cool to limit disciplines by not allowing innovative uses. I would say in general yes, for extremely outlandish uses if you want to use it regularly in a certain way (like the self imposition of a condition) a devotion is the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said in my original post, if you can come up with a creative way to utilize the power, have at it. It's just that you can't change the power's actual functions without creating a Devotion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers?p=974607#post974607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, for a sudden flash of genius - like a player trying the above in a moment of desperation, or using celerity to check the pistol in a game of Russian roulette with no-one noticing,</div> </div> </div> </div>That would seem to me to be within the scope of Celerity already in my opinion, since Celerity allows you to move faster than the eye can normally track for short bursts. Therefore, this would fall under clever application of the power's functions, not changing the power's functions. So I'd allow it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers?p=974607#post974607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or obfuscate to hide the taste of your blood in a rival's wine - I would encourage them to be creative, charging them at most a willpower for the improvisation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on who you ask, you might not even need to bother disguising the taste in your rival's wine because Vitae tastes good and that apparently is enough to not arouse suspicion. Though, I am in the &quot;just because it tastes good doesn't mean it's not suspicious&quot; camp. Regardless, here you're using a power that hides things you touch from perceptions in order to hide your blood from a single sense. Changing the the capabilities of the power, though it is an edge case, and I could see an argument for hiding the blood from all senses working just as well. That said, sense-selective Touch of Shadow would be an extremely cool and broadly useful Devotion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:09:36-07:00","id":974652,"title":"","content":"Again - more power! I err to permissiveness in the first instance, devotion costs for regular use - as it saves me having to look up in the book/have a debate in the middle of the game as to what is exactly possible within the purview. But this nuanced approach is probably very close to what I would come up with after allowing the initial one-off use in the middle of a game.<br /> <br /> But yes; no Dominating the power of gravity so you can fly. And no Nightmare 4 to recreate invisibility, as that's too close to obfuscate. But I did, for example, let celerity make a sneak attack in the middle of an ongoing fight by paying the vitae to run behind the attacker; and I would demand a devotion was paid for if this was to be used regularly in the middle of a duel.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:31:28-07:00","id":974667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers?p=974595#post974595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct, except through the Devotion <i>Chain of Command</i>, and even then it's technically Vampire A giving the command, just using Vampire B as a proxy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just looked over chain of command again. it allows Vampire A to make Vampire B give Vampire C A's command. Just like it said however I strongly believe that Vampire A has crushed Vampire B's will and made it their own... If vampire A dominated B and told B to get to C.... But to do that, vampire B had to go through D and E... I dont see why vampire B couldnt dominate them to make them go away or let him pass. Because he could Crush their will with his own desires...<br /> <br /> People who are often pushed over by 1 person are able to push over another person. but not the first person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:31:51-07:00","id":974668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers?p=974652#post974652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again - more power! I err to permissiveness in the first instance, devotion costs for regular use - as it saves me having to look up in the book/have a debate in the middle of the game as to what is exactly possible within the purview. But this nuanced approach is probably very close to what I would come up with after allowing the initial one-off use in the middle of a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's totally fair. I have a pretty deep familiarity with the Disciplines and what they do or don't do by default, so this isn't typically an issue for me, but that's a very good reason to rule in the player's favor in the moment and make a more permanent decision later, when it won't interrupt narrative flow. Good call.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/974509-how-flexible-are-kindred-powers?p=974652#post974652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes; no Dominating the power of gravity so you can fly. And no Nightmare 4 to recreate invisibility, as that's too close to obfuscate. But I did, for example, let celerity make a sneak attack in the middle of an ongoing fight by paying the vitae to run behind the attacker; and I would demand a devotion was paid for if this was to be used regularly in the middle of a duel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celerity surprise attacks are also already within the scope of the Discipline without a Devotion. I wouldn't allow it mI'd-combat, personally (with or without a Devotion), but yeah, that's a fine call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}